        "start": 23,
        "end": 33,
        "text": "The elements of a vector space are called vectors, and we will sometimes use the column matrix notation\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{c}\nz_{1}  \\tag{2.1}\\\\\n\\vdots\\\\\nz_{n}\n\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nto indicate a vector."
      },
      {
        "file": "/home/arnold/arnold/github/notes-helper/backend/projects/0728ff4c758a/refs/textbook.md",
        "start": 73,
        "end": 84,
        "text": "The standard quantum mechanical notation for a vector in a vector space is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{equation*}\n|\\psi\\rangle .\n\\tag{2.4}\n\\end{equation*}\n$$\n\n$\\psi$ is a label for the vector (any label is valid, although we prefer to use simple labels like $\\psi$ and $\\varphi$ ).\nThe $|\\cdot\\rangle$ notation is used to indicate that the object is a vector.\nThe entire object $|\\psi\\rangle$ is sometimes called a ket, although we won't use that terminology often."
      }
