    "id": "i7",
    "chunks": [
      {
        "file": "/home/arnold/arnold/github/notes-helper/backend/projects/0728ff4c758a/refs/textbook.md",
        "start": 132,
        "end": 155,
        "text": "For example, a spanning set for the vector space $\\mathbf{C}^{2}$ is the set\n\n$$\n\\left|v_{1}\\right\\rangle \\equiv\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n1  \\tag{2.5}\\\\\n0\n\\end{array}\\right] ; \\quad\\left|v_{2}\\right\\rangle \\equiv\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n0 \\\\n1\n\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nsince any vector\n\n$$\n|v\\rangle=\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\na_{1}  \\tag{2.6}\\\\\na_{2}\n\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nin $\\mathbf{C}^{2}$ can be written as a linear combination $|v\\rangle=a_{1}\\left|v_{1}\\right\\rangle+a_{2}\\left|v_{2}\\right\\rangle$ of the vectors $\\left|v_{1}\\right\\rangle$ and $\\left|v_{2}\\right\\rangle$.\nWe say that the vectors $\\left|v_{1}\\right\\rangle$ and $\\left|v_{2}\\right\\rangle$ span the vector space $\\mathbf{C}^{2}$."
