    "chunks": [
      {
        "file": "/home/arnold/arnold/github/notes-helper/backend/projects/0728ff4c758a/refs/textbook.md",
        "start": 217,
        "end": 219,
        "text": "Suppose $V, W$, and $X$ are vector spaces, and $A: V \\rightarrow W$ and $B: W \\rightarrow X$ are linear operators.\nThen we use the notation $B A$ to denote the composition of $B$ with $A$, defined by $(B A)(|v\\rangle) \\equiv B(A(|v\\rangle))$.\nOnce again, we write $B A|v\\rangle$ as an abbreviation for $(B A)(|v\\rangle)$."
      }
