        "start": 651,
        "end": 657,
        "text": "The tensor product is a way of putting vector spaces together to form larger vector spaces.\nThis construction is crucial to understanding the quantum mechanics of multiparticle systems.\nThe following discussion is a little abstract, and may be difficult to follow if you're not already familiar with the tensor product, so feel free to skip ahead now and revisit later when you come to the discussion of tensor products in quantum mechanics.\n\nSuppose $V$ and $W$ are vector spaces of dimension $m$ and $n$ respectively.\nFor convenience we also suppose that $V$ and $W$ are Hilbert spaces.\nThen $V \\otimes W$ (read '$V$ tensor $W$') is an $m n$ dimensional vector space."
