        "start": 702,
        "end": 705,
        "text": "The elements of $V \\otimes W$ are linear combinations of 'tensor products' $|v\\rangle \\otimes|w\\rangle$ of elements $|v\\rangle$ of $V$ and $|w\\rangle$ of $W$.\nIn particular, if $|i\\rangle$ and $|j\\rangle$ are orthonormal bases for the spaces $V$ and $W$ then $|i\\rangle \\otimes|j\\rangle$ is a basis for $V \\otimes W$.\nWe often use the abbreviated notations $|v\\rangle|w\\rangle,|v, w\\rangle$ or even $|v w\\rangle$ for the tensor product\n$|v\\rangle \\otimes|w\\rangle$."
