        "text": "There are many important functions which can be defined for operators and matrices.\nGenerally speaking, given a function $f$ from the complex numbers to the complex numbers, it is possible to define a corresponding matrix function on normal matrices (or some subclass, such as the Hermitian matrices) by the following construction.\nLet $A=\\sum_{a} a|a\\rangle\\langle a|$ be a spectral decomposition for a normal operator $A$.\nDefine $f(A) \\equiv \\sum_{a} f(a)|a\\rangle\\langle a|$.\nA little thought shows that $f(A)$ is uniquely defined."
